Start
/ Host plang on Windows: makes sure WSL and the PlangOS distro exist, then opens PlangOS.
/ Runs in the PlangOS folder (image\, distro\). Programs start through the terminal module;
/ each one outside the app root asks once: "Allow User to execute ...? (y/n/a)".
/ start.ps1 checks the image's sha256 against the manifest before plang runs (for now: file.read
/ returns a reference and crypto.hash doesn't give the file's hex sha256 yet on app-systems).
- run terminal 'wsl.exe' with parameters '--status', env WSL_UTF8=1, write to %wsl%
- if %wsl!exitCode% is not 0, call InstallWsl, then end goal
- read 'image/manifest-amd64.json', write to %manifest%
- run terminal 'wsl.exe' with parameters '--list', '--quiet', env WSL_UTF8=1, write to %distros%
- if %distros% contains 'PlangOS', call CheckImage
- if %distros% does not contain 'PlangOS', call ImportImage
- call OpenPlangOS

OpenPlangOS
/ PlangOS's Screen app runs a browser inside the container; its frames come up the pipe (stdout)
/ straight to our window — no goal per frame; our window's mouse and keyboard go down it (stdin),
/ one JSON line per event.
- open screen titled 'PlangOS desktop', size 1920x1080, on input call Input, on close call Close, write to %screen%
/ Formal: in words, the builder took the 'Screen' among the parameters for a goal to call on every
/ message (60 a second, a goal that doesn't exist: "Screen" in the console, and the pipe held up).
- terminal.open(App="wsl.exe", Parameter=["-d", "PlangOS", "--cd", "/home/plang", "--exec", "/opt/plang/plang", "Screen"], Binary=true, OutputTo=%screen%); variable.set(Name=%container%, Value=%!data%)
- wait for %container%

Input
- send %!data% to %container%

Close
- stop %container%

CheckImage
/ WSL keeps an imported distro's disk as distro\ext4.vhdx. distro\<sha256>.imported names the
/ image that disk came from, so no value comparison is needed.
/ file.exists gives the path; the path's own truth is whether the file is there.
- check if file 'distro/ext4.vhdx' exists, write to %ours%
- if %ours%, call CheckVersion, else call NotOurs

CheckVersion
- check if file 'distro/%manifest.sha256%.imported' exists, write to %current%
- if %current%, call Installed, else call ReplaceImage

Installed
- write out 'PlangOS %manifest.version% is installed'

NotOurs
- throw error 'A WSL distro named PlangOS exists, but this folder did not import it (no distro/ext4.vhdx). Remove it with: wsl --unregister PlangOS, then run start.ps1 again.'

InstallWsl
/ Needs administrator rights, and usually a reboot. RunOnce brings us back after login.
- write out 'Installing WSL. Windows will ask for administrator rights.'
- run terminal 'wsl.exe' with parameters '--install', '--no-distribution', as administrator, write to %install%
- if %install!exitCode% is not 0, call InstallFailed, then end goal
- run terminal 'reg.exe' with parameters 'add', 'HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\RunOnce', '/v', 'PlangOS', '/t', 'REG_SZ', '/f', '/d', 'powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -NoExit -File start.ps1', write to %runOnce%
- write out 'Restart Windows. PlangOS continues when you log back in.'

InstallFailed
- write out 'WSL install failed (exit %install!exitCode%).'
- write out 'Error 0x80370102 means virtualization is off in BIOS/UEFI. WSL needs Windows 10 build 19041 or later.'

ReplaceImage
/ A new image: remove the old distro, then import. /home/plang is not carried over yet.
- write out 'New PlangOS image %manifest.version%: replacing the installed one.'
/ A PlangOS still running (an earlier window) can make --unregister hang: stop it first. Neither
/ may hang the start: if WSL doesn't answer, say so and stop.
- terminal.start(App="wsl.exe", Parameter=["--terminate", "PlangOS"], Environment={"WSL_UTF8": 1}); on.timeout(After="PT1M"); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="WslStuck")]); variable.set(Name=%stopped%, Value=%!data%)
- terminal.start(App="wsl.exe", Parameter=["--unregister", "PlangOS"], Environment={"WSL_UTF8": 1}); on.timeout(After="PT2M"); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="WslStuck")]); variable.set(Name=%removed%, Value=%!data%)
- call ImportImage

WslStuck
- throw error 'WSL is not answering: PlangOS would not stop. Restart Windows, then run start.ps1 again.'

ImportImage
- write out 'Importing PlangOS %manifest.version%'
- run terminal 'wsl.exe' with parameters '--import', 'PlangOS', 'distro', 'image/%manifest.file%', '--version', '2', env WSL_UTF8=1, write to %import%
- if %import!exitCode% is not 0, call ImportFailed, then end goal
- save 'PlangOS %manifest.version%' to 'distro/%manifest.sha256%.imported'

ImportFailed
- write out 'wsl --import failed (exit %import!exitCode%): %import% %import!error%'
